 When a property's schema is a `$ref` to a shared definition, a `[PII]` marker on that definition applies to the property. Chronicle uses the definition's compliance metadata when it writes, releases and compares values.
 
-Pointer references such as `#/$defs/Name` resolve exactly as before. Only when a reference does not resolve that way does Chronicle look for an embedded `$id` resource or a `$anchor` in the same schema document. An anchor is scoped to the resource that declares it, so identically named anchors in different resources do not collide.
