 ---
 
-The Chronicle client creates spans for the work it does inside your application: appending events, committing a unit of work, and handling an event in a reactor or a reducer. Those spans are emitted on an activity source named `Cratis.Chronicle.Client`, and an OpenTelemetry tracer provider only records a source it has been told about. If you never register it, nothing is recorded, nothing fails, and the spans are simply missing from your traces.
+Register `AddCratisChronicleInstrumentation()` to trace Chronicle .NET client operations inside your application with OpenTelemetry. The client creates spans, timed records of operations, for event appends, unit-of-work commits and event handling in reactors and reducers.
 
-One call registers it: `AddCratisChronicleInstrumentation()`.
+These spans come from the activity source `Cratis.Chronicle.Client`. OpenTelemetry only records sources registered with its tracer provider; omitting this source produces no warning, just missing client spans.
 
-This page is about the client in your application. The Chronicle server exports its own telemetry; see [Open Telemetry](/chronicle/hosting/configuration/open-telemetry/) for that.
+Configure this instrumentation in your application host. To collect the kernel's telemetry as well, configure [server OpenTelemetry](/chronicle/hosting/configuration/open-telemetry/) separately.
 
